# Try it

[Download Siplicity for Windows (64-bit x64) - v0.0.2 (2026-09-22)](https://sipli.city/releases/siplicity_0.0.2.0.msix) 

Siplicity can be downloaded and tested for free. A license is required to use the *Commit* function.

# Buy it

An early access version* of Siplicity is now available for purchase.

Siplicity is licensed under the [Fair Core License](https://fcl.dev/). This means that users receive access to Siplicity's source code and can modify the application and distribute those modifications for use by other licensed users. It also means that [Siplicity automatically transitions to Open Source (Apache 2.0) after two years](https://github.com/sipli-city/siplicity-foss).

Licenses are a one-time purchase, valid for two years' worth of updates*, and don't expire (i.e. you can continue to use Siplicity if you don't renew, but won't have access to the latest releases). Licenses are issued on a per-user basis. 

```=html
<a href="#" class="button" onclick="openCheckout(itemsList)">Buy Siplicity</a>
```

**During the early access period, licenses remain continually valid, and will only need to be renewed two years after the release of version 1.0.*

